    "question": {
        "name": "CSEC Phy May 2022 Q1d — U-235 Fission Energy (Atomic Mass Units)",
        "text": "<p>The equation below represents a nuclear fission reaction:</p><p style='text-align:center;'>\\({}^{235}_{92}\\text{U} + {}^{1}_{0}\\text{n} \\rightarrow {}^{90}_{36}\\text{Kr} + {}^{144}_{56}\\text{Ba} + 2{}^{1}_{0}\\text{n} + \\text{energy}\\)</p><p>Using the atomic mass data in Table 2, calculate the <strong>energy released</strong> in the reaction. State your answer in joules.</p><table border='1' style='border-collapse:collapse; text-align:center; width:55%; margin:0.5em auto;'><tr><th>Nuclide</th><th>Atomic Mass / u</th></tr><tr><td>\\({}^{235}_{92}\\text{U}\\)</td><td>235.118</td></tr><tr><td>\\({}^{144}_{56}\\text{Ba}\\)</td><td>143.881</td></tr><tr><td>\\({}^{90}_{36}\\text{Kr}\\)</td><td>89.847</td></tr><tr><td>\\({}^{1}_{0}\\text{n}\\)</td><td>1.009</td></tr></table><p>[where u = 1.66 × 10⁻²⁷ kg &nbsp;|&nbsp; c = 3.0 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹] (7 marks)</p>",
        "general_feedback": "<p><strong>Reactants:</strong> m(U) + m(n) = 235.118 + 1.009 = 236.127 u<br><strong>Products:</strong> m(Kr) + m(Ba) + 2×m(n) = 89.847 + 143.881 + 2×1.009 = 89.847 + 143.881 + 2.018 = 235.746 u<br><strong>Mass defect:</strong> Δm = 236.127 − 235.746 = 0.381 u<br><strong>Convert to kg:</strong> 0.381 × 1.66×10⁻²⁷ = 6.3246×10⁻²⁸ kg<br><strong>Energy:</strong> E = Δm × c² = 6.3246×10⁻²⁸ × 9.0×10¹⁶ = <strong>5.69 × 10⁻¹¹ J</strong></p>"
    },
